1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,120
Your branch is behind main.

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,350
You can merge it, or you can rebase it.

3
00:00:06,317 --> 00:00:10,087
A merge adds one new commit
that joins the two histories.

4
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:15,900
A rebase takes your commits off your
branch and adds them again on top of main,

5
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:17,980
one after the other.

6
00:00:18,917 --> 00:00:21,687
These are new commits,
so they get new hashes.

7
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:26,680
So don't rebase a branch that
other people have already pulled.

8
00:00:27,025 --> 00:00:29,375
Their copy still has the old commits.

9
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:33,513
A merge keeps the history
the way it happened.

10
00:00:33,763 --> 00:00:36,073
A rebase turns it into a straight line,

11
00:00:36,443 --> 00:00:37,933
which is easier to read.

